worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_20.js"
  ceiling 1331
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver. The synchronous handler capability bindings moved to formal_ai_worker_dispatch.js; this shard keeps orchestration, the issue #710 browser parity recoveries, and since issue #1138 B8 / plan 09 leaves 13-15 the worker handler registry: the exact-permutation mirror of data/seed/handler-precedence.lino that binds the seed vocabulary (verifiable_task included) to worker implementations, which is why the ceiling moved from 1308 to 1459. Plan 09 leaf 41 then grew it to 1465: the registry permutation now reads the `handler <name>` row ids that carry the rank links instead of raw child names, mirroring MethodRegistry::from_store. The comment and call were re-compressed (1461) and the ceiling re-baselined to that measured value; the growth is the leaf-41 id-and-rank read, not silent regrowth. Ceiling re-baselined to 1345 with the bulk QA batch: the fourteen new precedence rows (summarization_text, text_rewrite, word_problem, the nine code-task handlers, statistics, unit_conversion) each gained their native-only registry key, which the exact-permutation assertion requires — without them loadSeed threw inside its catch and every seed-driven worker surface silently went empty. Ceiling moved 1345 to 1413 under the 2026-10-06 JavaScript-first doctrine (R997-R999): every native-only registry row is now bound to its JavaScript twin, and the fallback guard keeps the canned web-search paragraph out of answers (#1173 R5). Ceiling moved 1413 to 1442 for the 2026-10-06 meta-algorithm doctrine: solve() opens every turn with the recursive meta reasoner, hands a handler's admitted impasse to it, and finalize attaches the derivation to every answer. Ceiling moved 1442 to 1445: solve() imports learned meta chunks from memory and attaches newly learned ones as the answer's memory operation (R1007). Ceiling moved 1445 to 1446 for server parity (R1013): finalize attaches the native solver event log (`solverEvents`, built in formal_ai_worker_solver_events.js) so the JavaScript server narrates the trace Rust narrates. Ceiling moved 1446 to 1447: a bare imperative after earlier turns (a follow-up refining their artifact) never takes the turn through the early meta answer. Ceiling moved 1447 to 1455: +5 for the issue #1175 routing-probe ports (the inline response-language demonstration after the follow-up replay and the inline how_it_works mechanism plan after the async lookups, both through formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js) and +3 for the R1013 programExecution passthrough in finalize. Ceiling lowered 1455 to 1331: the issue #999 warning band (1400) moved the formalization fold-back, interpretation, deformalization and thinking-level helpers, unchanged, to formal_ai_worker_formalization_support.js."
